            <ArticleTitle>Hydrogen-Bonding Interactions in Luminescent Quinoline-Triazoles with Dominant 1D Crystals.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">E1600</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3390/molecules22101600</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Quinoline-triazoles 2-((4-(diethoxymethyl)-1H-1,2,3-triazol-1-yl)methyl)quinoline (1), 2-((4-(m-tolyl)-1H-1,2,3-triazol-1-yl)methyl)quinoline (2) and 2-((4-(p-tolyl)-1H-1,2,3-triazol-1-yl)methyl)quinoline (3) have been prepared with CuAAC click reactions and used as a model series to probe the relationship between lattice H-bonding interaction and crystal direction of growth. Crystals of 1-3 are 1D tape and prism shapes that correlate with their intermolecular and solvent 1D lattice H-bonding interactions. All compounds were thermally stable up to about 200 C and blue-green emissive in solution.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
